        "original_id": "edfa492f-9ddb-5be4-8bcb-116dfdea3507",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Allen Drury, Philip K. Dick\n- Works: Advise and Consent, The Throne of Saturn\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\n- Topics: American novelists, science fiction, political novels, Mars missions\n\nFacts:\n- Allen Drury was born on September 2, 1918, and was an American novelist.\n- Philip K. Dick was born on December 16, 1928, and was an American writer notable for publishing science fiction.\n- Allen Drury wrote the 1959 novel \"Advise and Consent.\"\n- Allen Drury won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction in 1960 for \"Advise and Consent.\"\n- Allen Drury wrote the 1971 science fiction and political novel \"The Throne of Saturn.\"\n- \"The Throne of Saturn\" explores preparations for a near-future manned mission to Mars.\n- Philip K. Dick died on March 2, 1982.\n- Allen Drury died on September 2, 1998.",
